Reports stopped being generated four days ago. The web application has been healthy throughout and no alert fired.

```csharp
public class ReportSweeper : BackgroundService
{
    private readonly SupportContext _db;

    public ReportSweeper(SupportContext db) => _db = db;

    protected override async Task ExecuteAsync(CancellationToken stoppingToken)
    {
        while (!stoppingToken.IsCancellationRequested)
        {
            var due = await _db.ReportJobs
                .Where(j => j.Status == "pending")
                .ToListAsync(stoppingToken);

            foreach (var job in due) await BuildAsync(job, stoppingToken);

            await Task.Delay(TimeSpan.FromMinutes(1), stoppingToken);
        }
    }
}
```

Name the two defects, and say which one explains the silence.

solution.code:
function dueJobs(jobs, now) {
  const due = jobs.filter(j => j.enabled === true && j.nextRunAt <= now);
  return due.map(j => j.id);
}

grading.starterCode:
function dueJobs(jobs, now) {
  // Enabled, and scheduled at or before now.
  return jobs.map(j => j.id);
}

