The Node service had a module-level cache that worked without incident for two years:

```ts
const cache: Record<string, Team> = {};

export function getTeam(id: string): Team | undefined {
  return cache[id];
}

export function putTeam(team: Team): void {
  cache[team.id] = team;
}
```

Translated to C#:

```csharp
public static class TeamCache
{
    private static readonly Dictionary<string, Team> Cache = new();

    public static Team? Get(string id) =>
        Cache.TryGetValue(id, out var team) ? team : null;

    public static void Put(Team team) => Cache[team.id] = team;
}
```

Under load the service occasionally pins a CPU core at 100% and stops responding. What changed?
